; qOS trusted-base SELinux confinement (CIL).
; ===========================================================================
; Confines the collaborative filesystem daemon (fs.service) into its own
; SELinux domain instead of the catch-all unconfined_service_t it lands in
; today (a custom binary with no policy = no MAC confinement). This is the
; MAC backstop for the trusted base: if fs is ever compromised, the kernel
; still boxes it.
;
; POSTURE: permissive-first.
; --------------------------
; The system runs SELinux ENFORCING and fs currently works. fs does a lot
; (FUSE mount of /var/workspace, iroh P2P networking, blob I/O under
; /var/cache, a unix control socket the compositor talks to), so the precise
; enforcing allow-set can only be finalised by capturing live AVCs on a real
; run. Shipping an incomplete ENFORCING domain would break a working daemon;
; shipping it PERMISSIVE logs every access without blocking, so fs keeps
; working AND we collect exactly the AVCs needed to tighten to enforcing.
; This is the standard SELinux bring-up workflow (permissive -> audit2allow ->
; enforcing), and is an honest improvement over unconfined_service_t.
;
; HOW fs ENTERS THE DOMAIN
; ------------------------
; fs.service carries `SELinuxContext=system_u:system_r:qos_fs_t:s0` (drop-in),
; so systemd setexeccon's into qos_fs_t at exec — no binary relabel needed
; (the executable stays bin_t; qos_fs_t is allowed to entrypoint bin_t). The
; init_t -> qos_fs_t transition is allowed explicitly (init_t is enforcing).

(type qos_fs_t)
(typeattributeset domain (qos_fs_t))
(roletype system_r qos_fs_t)

; Permissive: log-but-allow everything qos_fs_t does while the enforcing
; allow-set is being established from real AVCs.
(typepermissive qos_fs_t)

; Let init (systemd) transition fs into the domain and entrypoint the binary
; (which keeps its default bin_t label — no relabel in the image).
(allow init_t qos_fs_t (process (transition)))
(allow qos_fs_t bin_t (file (entrypoint execute execute_no_trans read open getattr map ioctl)))
(allow init_t qos_fs_t (process (siginh rlimitinh noatsecure)))

; ENFORCING HARDENING PATH (do after a VM run captures AVCs):
; -----------------------------------------------------------
; 1. boot, exercise fs (mount /var/workspace, read/write, peer sync),
;    then: `ausearch -m AVC -ts boot | audit2allow -C` (or audit2allow -M).
; 2. translate the generated allow rules into CIL allows on qos_fs_t here
;    (fuse, the iroh sockets, /var/workspace + /var/cache file types, the
;    control socket, capabilities), replacing `(typepermissive qos_fs_t)`.
; 3. drop the permissive line so qos_fs_t enforces.
; The compositor (shell) runs in the greetd session domain; giving it its own
; confined domain is the next base-daemon target, same workflow.
